{"purpose":"Define v1.x product requirements and MVP scope for standalone release orchestration toolkit. Historical baseline for traceability.","content":"PRD-001 Anvil — Runtime \u0026 Release Orchestration Toolkit. Product requirements for Anvil as universal orchestration layer between projects and platforms. Defines product vision (between projects/platforms/frameworks/environments), problem statement (reinvented release management, framework lock-in, vocabulary), philosophy (documentation first, platform over project, convention with explicit config, framework agnostic), principles, goals, users, use cases (init, package, verify, activate, rollback, pipeline, inspect, cleanup), scope (release management, activation lifecycle, pipeline, config, state, CLI), MVP scope, out-of-scope, success criteria, roadmap phases Foundation→Release Engine→Pipeline Engine→Adapter Ecosystem→Enterprise→Platform. Status Draft 2026-07-19. Superseded for v2 by PRD-002 2026-08-03 but preserved as historical v1.x baseline. See docs/prd/PRD-001-anvil.md."}